&lt;p&gt;As a Growth Data Scientist, you will use data to help shape how ERGO NEXT reaches, serves, and converts customers across our &lt;strong&gt;partnership channel&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;customer experience funnel&lt;/strong&gt;. You will work closely with Product and Partnerships teams to identify growth opportunities, understand customer behavior, and turn insights into product and business decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who combines strong analytical and statistical skills with business judgment, curiosity, and a bias toward action. You should be comfortable working through ambiguous questions, developing a point of view, and using both traditional data science methods and emerging AI capabilities to make analysis more scalable, efficient, and impactful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI as part of the day-to-day data science workflow and identify opportunities to develop reusable AI-enabled tools, skills, or agents that solve practical analytical and business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategy and roadmap for the Partnership channel and the customer experience funnel through actionable data insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own analytics for the entire customer experience funnel, from acquired opportunities to purchases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evaluate experiments and causal analyses to measure the impact of product, funnel, and customer experience changes and guide future strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze affiliates performance across the partnership channel, identifying differences in traffic quality, conversion, product mix, and customer behavior to uncover opportunities to improve partner growth and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, size, and prioritize growth opportunities, translating ambiguous business questions into rigorous analyses and actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply statistical analysis, segmentation, modeling, and deep-dive analysis to understand the underlying drivers of business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define clear metrics, measurement frameworks, and visualizations to help business monitor performance and make data driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[4+] years of experience in Data Science or other highly quantitative analytical roles (experience working in fintech or growth &amp;amp; partnerships is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn new AI capabilities, identify meaningful gaps in existing workflows, and apply or develop practical AI-enabled solutions that improve how data science work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in SQL and experience using Python or R for statistical analysis and analytical workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in statistics, experimentation, and causal inference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with experiment design, implementation, analysis, and recommendation for actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to define the appropriate metric framework to empower the data-driven decision-making process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to translate complex analyses into clear recommendations and influence cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing customer journeys, conversion funnels, or growth with the ability to connect changes in metrics to underlying business drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with partnership or other multi-channel business models, with the ability to evaluate partner performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
