&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help us build a development lifecycle where AI agents work alongside every engineer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Developer Experience (DevEx) team builds the tools, platforms and automation that make ERGO NEXT engineers more productive. We’re looking for an experienced Software Engineer who is a developer first: you’ve built and shipped production software, you know what slows engineers down because you’ve felt it yourself, and you’re comfortable working with CI/CD, cloud and Kubernetes. You’ll take a key part in building our Agentic (AI-based) Software Development Life Cycle, where AI agents assist in designing, coding, testing and deploying our services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want your code to change how an entire engineering organization works, we’d like to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the tools, platforms and automation that make our engineers more productive, treating our platform as a product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a key part in building our Agentic SDLC, applying AI agents to every step from design and coding to testing and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the full spectrum of cloud and applicative infrastructure, including CI/CD, Kubernetes, Terraform and AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with developers to understand the challenges our platform needs to solve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate, plan and lead projects that improve developers’ day-to-day work and help them bring value to the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track adoption and impact of what you build, and iterate based on developer feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
