&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Owner&#39;s Policy is our flagship product, and this squad owns it. Today it&#39;s run by insurance product managers carrying both the insurance and the technology load. We&#39;re hiring a PM to take the technology and GTM half: roadmap, technical solutions, delivery, packaging, design, and channel go-to-market. The IPMs stay the authority on the insurance product itself, from underwriting guidelines to new coverages, limits, and industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One key part of this job is using AI to grow the product relentlessly. That means AI in the GTM, AI that makes everyone in the squad work more efficiently together, and building tools that help the team build the insurance product itself. We don&#39;t care where the leverage comes from. We care that you find it, and that the squad moves faster and the product gets better every month because you&#39;re on it, using AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You, insurance product managers, along with the rest of the squad carry the same OKRs. That means you&#39;re accountable for knowing the insurance product well enough to make sound decisions about how to grow it, not just for shipping what&#39;s handed to you. If you want to work on financial products with real revenue (in the $xxxM range), a complex and interesting technical surface, and massive ceiling to change how it continues to get built, this is the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive the roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; You are responsible for making sure that&amp;nbsp; sizings get done, and make the long-term versus short-term trade-off explicit rather than implied. You and insurance product managers agree on the plan together; you&#39;re ultimately accountable for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship a true Business Owner’s Policy (BOP) product.&lt;/strong&gt; Take a bundled product that customers understand and buy in a single flow, and close the distance between what we sell today and what makes a great BOP product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own go-to-market with the channels.&lt;/strong&gt; NEXT distribute our insurance products through 3&amp;nbsp; channels: Direct, Agent, and Partnership. You will work closely with the cross-functional groups to focus and deliver on a plan of action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Package and merchandise products.&lt;/strong&gt; How coverage is presented and packaged to small business owners and to insurance agents are a product decision, and it&#39;s yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build a great user experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Build delightful UX that drives conversion increase and underwriting quality improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run planning and executive communication.&lt;/strong&gt; Run product strategy planning and host monthly progress update and strategy discussion session with the executive team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn insurance.&lt;/strong&gt; Coverages, appetite, filings, loss ratio and more. You won&#39;t be the authority on it, but you will be fluent, and the squad will feel it if you aren&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in product management, shipping customer-facing products with meaningful revenue attached. Bonus if that product was complex, regulated, or financial, where the details are the hard part&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User obsession backed by ruthless prioritization. You understand your user&#39;s pain points well enough to cut the roadmap down to the few things that actually change their experience, and you stay focused on delivering that impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive communication. You can compress a complex situation into something a VP and chief executives understand clearly and respond to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working with distribution channels or GTM teams. You&#39;ve been the pseudo-PMM for a product before, or close to it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort building software that sells a complex, regulated, or financial product where the details matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of challenging the status quo by getting to the core of a problem, not by having stronger opinions or louder voice than everyone else in the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use AI tools to accelerate and automate your workflows without compromising quality and critical thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unstoppable Qualities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in insurance, fintech, lending, or another regulated category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to small businesses, where the buyer is the owner and the attention span is thirty seconds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience. You have deep experience working directly with data, as well as working with data sciences partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong design partnership instincts. You brief well and you know when the answer is a UX problem, not a feature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range displayed on this job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire base salaries for the position in the location(s) listed. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including, without limitation, job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. ERGO NEXT employees are also potentially eligible for our annual performance-based incentive program, in addition to our benefits package, consisting of our partially subsidized medical plan, fully subsidized vision/dental options, life insurance, disability insurance, 401(k), flexible paid time off, parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;US annual base salary range for this full-time position:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Palo Alto, CA: $180,000 - $244,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Waltham, MA: $163,000 - $220,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
